From 5da401b8f2310de64669c67c808e6f54b09955d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:05:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a status window saved as a title bar minimized

UI_MSG_SET_INFO for the status window first minimizes it when the saved
height differs from the saved full height. It then applies the saved
expanded state through ID_EXPAND, which resizes the window to 0x8d or
0xf1. The window therefore always reopens at full height, and the saved
title-bar state is never restored. The 2022-04-06 executable uses the
same order.

Minimize after applying the expanded state, so the title-bar toggle
also records the expanded height to restore.

Validation: the new test_status_wnd_info restores normal, expanded,
minimized, minimized-expanded and invalid saved layouts through the
extracted message handler, and checks a store-and-restore round trip;
it fails without the fix. Release build without warnings; the full
behavioral suite passed on the completed series.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
